          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Pyramid",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Unit",
                    "sub": "Vitest/Jest + RTL, many, fast",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Integration",
                    "sub": "a few",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "E2E",
                    "sub": "Playwright, critical flows only",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Jest vs Vitest",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Vitest",
                "Jest"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Built on",
                  "Vite, ==ESM-first==",
                  "`next/jest`, SWC transform"
                ],
                [
                  "Mock fn",
                  "`vi.fn`",
                  "`jest.fn`"
                ],
                [
                  "API",
                  "`describe`/`it`/`expect`",
                  "same"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. What to Test and Mock",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Async Server Components: ==E2E==, RTL cannot render them",
                "Or unit test their extracted pure logic",
                "Test what the user sees: ==roles and text==",
                "Not state, class names or internal calls",
                "Mock {red:network}, {red:DB}, `next/navigation`",
                "Never mock the component under test"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "vi.mock('next/navigation')",
                "render(<Save />)",
                "screen.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i })"
              ],
              "note": "mock the edge, query by role"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Boundary rule",
              "text": "Mock what is **outside** the component, never the component itself."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**RTL and async Server Components?** It cannot render them; use E2E or extracted logic.",
                "**What do you mock?** Network, DB, `next/navigation`; never the unit under test.",
                "**Vitest vs Jest?** Vitest is Vite-native with a Jest-like API (`vi.fn`)."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unit Tests with Jest or Vitest and RTL",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unit Tests with Jest or Vitest and RTL",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Setup",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Jest",
                "Vitest"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Install",
                  "`npm i -D jest jest-environment-jsdom @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom`",
                  "`npm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react jsdom @testing-library/react`"
                ],
                [
                  "Config",
                  "`jest.config.ts` with `createJestConfig` from `next/jest`",
                  "`vitest.config.mts` with plugins `[react()]`"
                ],
                [
                  "DOM",
                  "`testEnvironment: 'jsdom'`",
                  "`test.environment: 'jsdom'`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Test Pattern",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`render(<Comp />)`, then query with ==screen.getByRole==",
                "Assert with ==jest-dom== matchers like `toBeInTheDocument()`",
                "Use ==userEvent.setup()== and `await user.click(...)`, not `fireEvent`",
                "Async UI: ==findBy*== or `waitFor`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "render(<Save />)",
                "const user = userEvent.setup()",
                "await user.click(",
                "  screen.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i }))",
                "expect(await screen.findByText('Saved'))",
                "  .toBeInTheDocument()"
              ],
              "note": "query by role and name, like a user"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Run",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`npm test`",
                  "runs the `test` script in package.json"
                ],
                [
                  "`vitest run`",
                  "CI, single pass"
                ],
                [
                  "`vitest`",
                  "watch mode"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Add a ==test== script to package.json. Click with **userEvent** and `await` it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Testing Server Components and Server Actions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Testing Server Components and Server Actions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What RTL Can Render",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Target",
                "Unit test?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Sync Server Component",
                  "{green:Renders fine} with RTL"
                ],
                [
                  "Async Server Component",
                  "{red:Cannot render}: use ==Playwright=="
                ],
                [
                  "Extracted async function",
                  "{green:Yes}, mock `fetch`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Move the fetch/query out into a ==plain async function==",
                "Unit test that function with a mocked `fetch`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Server Actions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "An action is just an ==async function== marked `'use server'`",
                "Import it, call it with a `FormData`",
                "Mock `next/headers`, `next/cache`, `next/navigation` with `vi.mock` / `jest.mock`",
                "Real `redirect` throws ==NEXT_REDIRECT==, so mock it and assert the call"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "vi.mock('next/cache', () => ({ revalidatePath: vi.fn() }))",
                "vi.mock('next/navigation', () => ({ redirect: vi.fn() }))",
                "it('saves', async () => {",
                "  const fd = new FormData(); fd.set('title', 'Hi')",
                "  await createPost(fd)",
                "  expect(revalidatePath).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/posts')",
                "  expect(redirect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/posts')",
                "})"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Form Taking an Action Prop",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pass ==vi.fn()== as the `action` prop",
                "The form is tested without the server"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const action = vi.fn()",
                "const user = userEvent.setup()",
                "render(<PostForm action={action} />)",
                "await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i }))",
                "expect(action).toHaveBeenCalled()"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Async Server Component = ==Playwright==. Actions = plain functions with `FormData`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
